<p>NASA STD-8739.4 gives standards for wire harnesses, and tells us that at a wire diameter of 0.25 inches or less, maximum tie off distance should be 0.75 inches. While not all wire gauges have been decided, it is likely that most wries will end up smaller than 0.25 inches, so this requirement is applied to the entire rocket. This is decomposed from TVC-MO-007, where wires coming loose is considerd &quot;disassembly&quot;.</p>
